+- **Limitations:** Does not account for aspect ratio optimization; may waste memory if the AABB is highly elongated. Zero-extent axes are clamped to 1, which may not be desired for all applications [S2, unofficial].
+- **When to use:** When a uniform grid is required for spatial indexing of splats or points within a known bounding volume [G].
 
 ## Background
-Originating from implementations like `splatcarve` by stevekwon211, this method is used in 3D Gaussian Splatting pipelines to map splat centers to a discrete voxel grid for efficient carving and rendering [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the coordinate space setup defined in [Voxel Space Setup](3520-voxel-space-setup.md).
